## §5. GOVERNANCE & ACCEPTANCE

### Policy Drift Detection

Failures involving governance semantics MUST be classified as `policy_regression_fix`, not `production_bug_fix`.

**Policy drift triggers:** fail-closed vs fail-open behavior, approval/rejection logic, confidence thresholds, manual review routing, replay enforcement, side-effect guards, mutation gate bypass.

Evidence MUST include `## POLICY_DRIFT` section with: failing test, policy domain, intended vs observed behavior, winning contract, resolution layer, repair plan.

FORBIDDEN: patching assertion to match broken behavior; adjusting threshold to make test pass; classifying governance bug as `production_bug_fix`.

### Contract Conflict Escalation

When two rules require incompatible behavior from the same component: STOP, record `## CONTRACT_CONFLICT`, identify winning contract (lower L-number wins, constitutional rules win), name resolution layer. Do NOT resume repair until conflict resolved.

Patching around a contract conflict = HARD FAIL.

### Environment Parity

Local environment behavior is not valid CI behavior until an environment contract artifact proves parity.

Required when failure involves: subprocess execution, WSL/OS boundary, CUDA/GPU, HuggingFace/vLLM, import path manipulation, filesystem layout assumptions, network/external services.

Evidence MUST include `## ENVIRONMENT_CONTRACT` section. FORBIDDEN: fixing locally and declaring convergence before CI validation.

### Acceptance Criteria

Acceptance criteria MUST be deterministic, command-exact, exit-code-exact, count-exact. Forbidden language: "should", "expected to", "approximately", "equivalent". Criteria immutable once phase begins.

**Forbidden Overclaiming Vocabulary:**

| Forbidden claim | Required condition |
|---|---|
| "tests are present" | Raw ADG entity count `tests > 0` |
| "fixtures are present" | Raw ADG entity count `fixtures > 0` |
| "convergence achieved" | All five §7.2 conditions met |
| "repair complete" | All six §7.3 conditions met |
| "repo is healthy" | Post-repair full-suite green (zero fails, errors, unexpected skips) |
| "no dependencies" | ADG explicitly returned empty edge set |
| "directly observed" | Fact read directly from raw artifact — no inference |

### Convergence Declaration (Scoped Claim Only)

ALL five conditions must hold simultaneously:
1. Active scoped failures = 0
2. Unregistered skips = 0
3. No expired registry entries
4. `FACT_CLASSIFICATION.Unresolved` is empty
5. Scope lossiness documented (if file-level fallback used)

### Repair Run Completion (Six Conditions)

1. All §7.2 scoped convergence conditions met
2. Every ADG-reachable dependent of repaired surface executed and passed
3. Full pytest suite green — zero failures, errors, unexpected skips
4. Full-suite run timestamp LATER THAN last repair commit timestamp
5. No new failures introduced (count ≤ pre-repair baseline)
6. Final summary artifact in `docs/reports/plans/` with empty `Unresolved`

